<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101285" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῦρος</span></b> , ὁ,
			<u>Syros</u>, one of the Cyclades, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			10.5.8
		</span></i>; called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῠρίη</span></b>  in
			<i><span class="en">
			Od.
			15.403
		</span></i> (acc. to <i><span class="en">
			Str.
		</span></i> l.c.: but more probably <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῠρίη</span>
		is Sicily and the name is connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῠράκουσαι</span>); later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σύρα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Suid.
		</span></i>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φερεκύδης</span>
			, f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				1.119
			</span></i>:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σύριος</span></b> ,
				ὁ, <i>a Syrian,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12.193.32
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				1.116
			</span></i>.</div>
